WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.578 --> 00:00:03.248
- Well, I love painting the
maps because it gets me out

00:00:03.248 --> 00:00:04.081
in the weather like this.

00:00:04.081 --> 00:00:05.210
(camera clicks)

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:07.209
It's pretty awesome to come into a resort

00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:09.459
and look up and see my map.

00:00:11.087 --> 00:00:14.004
(enchanting music)

00:00:16.091 --> 00:00:18.587
I'm James Niehues, and
I've painted ski maps

00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:21.595
of some of the biggest
resorts around the world.

00:00:21.595 --> 00:00:24.262
I've painted 194 different maps.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.267
This is North Star out at Lake Tahoe.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.737
And a Mexico ski area.

00:00:30.737 --> 00:00:33.341
Then we have Snowbasin here in Utah.

00:00:33.341 --> 00:00:35.736
This is an image that skiers see.

00:00:35.736 --> 00:00:39.200
They judge the mountain by the trail map.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:43.704
You want to portray the
mountain as beautiful as it is.

00:00:43.704 --> 00:00:48.000
I was a advertising
agency man for awhile.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.831
In 1987, I painted my first trail map.

00:00:51.831 --> 00:00:53.410
They used my map.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:54.583
I loved it right away.

00:00:54.583 --> 00:00:56.011
I could paint and do a little travel,

00:00:56.011 --> 00:00:57.761
and learn how to ski.

00:00:59.842 --> 00:01:01.584
Whenever I get a call from a resort,

00:01:01.584 --> 00:01:03.728
the first thing that I'll
do is scope out the mountain

00:01:03.728 --> 00:01:06.098
and see what I've got to work with.

00:01:06.098 --> 00:01:08.943
I work heavily from aerial photography.

00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:11.810
Or I'll go up in a plane, I’ll
take a pan across the whole

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.393
mountain in a shot.

00:01:14.313 --> 00:01:17.030
From this, I take it back to the studio

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:19.572
and I get on my computer
and select the ones

00:01:19.572 --> 00:01:21.527
that I want to work from, print 'em out,

00:01:21.527 --> 00:01:24.406
and then I reference all
the material that I can get

00:01:24.406 --> 00:01:26.073
and start my sketch.

00:01:26.914 --> 00:01:28.911
What I will have to do is manipulate

00:01:28.911 --> 00:01:30.873
the different elements of the mountain

00:01:30.873 --> 00:01:33.462
and get it on a single plane of paper,

00:01:33.462 --> 00:01:34.879
on a single page.

00:01:35.882 --> 00:01:37.426
(bright music)

00:01:37.426 --> 00:01:39.307
What I like to do is show the skier

00:01:39.307 --> 00:01:41.059
what he's skiing through.

00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:44.762
And help the skier identify
where he is on the mountain.

00:01:44.762 --> 00:01:48.106
For a large ski resort,
it'll take me three weeks

00:01:48.106 --> 00:01:52.273
of painting, but that doesn't
include all your prep work.

00:01:53.191 --> 00:01:57.731
So realistically, it'll
take me three months.

00:01:57.731 --> 00:01:59.193
Do I have a favorite mountain?

00:01:59.193 --> 00:02:02.038
Wow, I've done a lot of them.

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:05.196
And a lot of really exciting mountains.

00:02:05.196 --> 00:02:08.284
There's a lot of things that
I love about doing this job.

00:02:08.284 --> 00:02:10.989
I get to fly in some of
the most beautiful spots

00:02:10.989 --> 00:02:12.072
in the world.

00:02:13.091 --> 00:02:16.674
I'm gonna keep doing
this as long as I can.

